  "question": {
    "text": "An electron from various excited states of hydrogen atom emit radiation to come to the ground state. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></math> be the de Broglie wavelength of the electron in the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> state and the ground state respectively. Let <math><msub><mrow><mo>&#8743;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></math> be the wavelength of the emitted photon in the transition from the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> state to the ground state. For large n, (A, B are constants)",
    "image": null
